		{
			"id": "110968004342049268",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110968004342049268",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T15:42:50.940Z",
			"content": "<p>Well—wait. Is it not well known that the end-game for Astro is almost certainly to sell the company?</p><p>They’ve taken $10M from investors—likely to result in the same funding problem that Gatsby had—except with (imo) an even larger risk as they don’t seem to have started monetization efforts.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968012104388814",
			"parentId": "110968004342049268",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110968012104388814",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T15:44:49.383Z",
			"content": "<p>Certainly not claiming that Eleventy’s problems or risks are better, just different.</p><p>We’ve taken $0 from investors, which is definitely easier for me to manage long-term (what I’m optimizing for).</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968036479326383",
			"parentId": "110968012104388814",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@bastianallgeier/110968036422722148",
			"author": {
				"name": "Bastian Allgeier",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@bastianallgeier",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/225/968/517/429/original/30c7078b2f8c4d75.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T15:51:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> In my experience, 95% of all VC funded competitors in our areas will vanish when you are playing the long-term game and just wait long enough. The other 5% will become so expensive that they end up as enterprise systems for a very exclusive audience.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968038929860767",
			"parentId": "110968004342049268",
			"url": "https://mstdn.social/@kixxauth/110968038841719622",
			"author": {
				"name": "Kris Walker",
				"url": "https://mstdn.social/@kixxauth",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/835/981/042/973/496/original/832faf6af375b9a6.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T15:51:37.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p><p>I guess I'm old school, but it twists my brain into a knot trying to understand the ecosystem around venture funded open source projects.</p><p>It's so counter to ... everything I've known about software up until 2019.</p><p>I guess, 20 years into the future, we'll see this as a strange blip.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968041350429730",
			"parentId": "110968038929860767",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110968041350429730",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T15:52:15.647Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mstdn.social/@kixxauth\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>kixxauth</span></a></span> would you call it a zero interest rate phenomenon</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968044127812430",
			"parentId": "110968012104388814",
			"url": "https://cosocial.ca/@boris/110968044060931634",
			"author": {
				"name": "Boris Mann",
				"url": "https://cosocial.ca/@boris",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/118/955/928/962/297/original/35ae22c59e006661.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T15:52:57.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I think “more well understood” would be fair. It’s an open source framework with an MIT license.</p><p>I assume you own some domain names and graphics and such, and otherwise it can be endlessly remixed for people to try alternate paths.</p><p>The hard work of maintenance and compatibility, never mind new features, docs, community management, gets done as much as people volunteer or are paid to do it.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968053860102039",
			"parentId": "110968004342049268",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@lekoarts/110968053756496102",
			"author": {
				"name": "Lennart",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@lekoarts",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/392/614/633/440/446/original/33add9f610e4b79c.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T15:55:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Maybe I'm out of the loop but I'd also like to know how they want to earn money, the initial post didn’t say <a href=\"https://astro.build/blog/the-astro-technology-company/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">astro.build/blog/the-astro-tec</span><span class=\"invisible\">hnology-company/</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968065525440217",
			"parentId": "110968044127812430",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110968065525440217",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T15:58:24.524Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://cosocial.ca/@boris\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>boris</span></a></span> I think the same could be said of Astro too, no? The framework is also open source/open licensed.</p><p>The nuance I’ve been thinking about is more FTE =&gt; biting off larger problems =&gt; larger code base =&gt; more maintenance risk when the company is sold.</p><p>Just for comparison I don’t think volunteers will maintain Gatsby given that the framework is owned by Netlify (and Netlify is laying off folks that used to do the job of maintaining Gatsby)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968067170837681",
			"parentId": "110968041350429730",
			"url": "https://mstdn.social/@kixxauth/110968067134531479",
			"author": {
