				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/291/886/080/250/362/original/533c7d9904760762.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T16:08:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> that is 100% why I will not use it. Because it is not upfront with how they intend to monetise.</p><p>It is so clear that they are intending to sell it to someone else. This feels extremely sour to me, because especially with these types of technologies, you are selling a community, or access to a community.</p><p>I didn't say anything because I thought I was just paranoid, but that is just how venture capitalism works, and they very much participate.</p><p>No shade to the devs, but it is a reality.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
