			"parentId": "110968818496169491",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110968845489353426",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T19:16:45.828Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@eliancodes\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>eliancodes</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@lekoarts\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>lekoarts</span></a></span> I think the concern here is that folks are worried that a VC-backed company without a monetization strategy is a pretty risky thing to bet on</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968953662674971",
			"parentId": "110968845489353426",
			"url": "https://c.im/@matthewp/110968953631849390",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matthew Phillips",
				"url": "https://c.im/@matthewp",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/319/884/743/792/129/original/97348f81981453d9.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T19:44:15.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@eliancodes\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eliancodes</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@lekoarts\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>lekoarts</span></a></span> Everything's perishable, right? With companies you worry that they might fail. With BDFL you worry about bus factor. A foundation is probably the safest place for a project, but even those seem to take on more than they can maintain. Good thing about SSG is that once you deploy you can throw away the framework you used to build it, if you want.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110969085549196285",
			"parentId": "110968417986750454",
			"url": "https://pleroma.envs.net/objects/6f4ba529-d580-4581-9a59-72b5057816ea",
			"private": true,
			"date": "2023-08-28T20:17:41.691Z",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110969353695427411",
			"parentId": "110968953662674971",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@lekoarts/110969353540826638",
			"author": {
				"name": "Lennart",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@lekoarts",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/392/614/633/440/446/original/33add9f610e4b79c.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T21:25:58.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://c.im/@matthewp\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>matthewp</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@eliancodes\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eliancodes</span></a></span> For my hobby projects I wouldn’t care, for my business I would care a lot.</p><p>Bit surprised to hear that there are no concrete plans, normally no one just gives money away for free.</p><p>Projects like Next, Astro, Gatsby, etc. are so complex, once no one gets paid anymore to work on them it’s impossible for the community to immediately pick it up unless preparations were made and non-company core contributors were taught.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110969400292083270",
			"parentId": "110969353695427411",
			"url": "https://c.im/@matthewp/110969400256566337",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matthew Phillips",
				"url": "https://c.im/@matthewp",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/319/884/743/792/129/original/97348f81981453d9.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T21:37:50.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@lekoarts\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>lekoarts</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@eliancodes\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eliancodes</span></a></span> There are concrete plans, but not ones I can share here now. Stay tuned.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110969416063986638",
			"parentId": "110968004342049268",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@benschwarz/110969415757872915",
			"author": {
				"name": "benschwarz",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@benschwarz",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/295/713/321/949/633/original/45e52f3c0901216e.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T21:41:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I’ve lamented similar previously too (<a href=\"https://twitter.com/benschwarz/status/1585482090971136001\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">twitter.com/benschwarz/status/</span><span class=\"invisible\">1585482090971136001</span></a>). Gatsby’s seed was $5m at a time when that was described by some as a “mango” seed round (yes, I know 🤮). </p><p>It sounds weird, but you can raise a bunch of money to get 3-5 years down the line, then side step to actual adults take over when it’s probably too late anyway. Tech never learns.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110969682037944437",
			"parentId": "110968012104388814",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@voxpelli/110969682007345189",
			"author": {
				"name": "Pelle Wessman",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@voxpelli",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/288/782/009/996/943/original/7631cc5a4e9dde08.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T22:49:30.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Eleventy is for sure more of a community project than these VC infused projects.</p><p>One reason I eg have staid away from Prisma, Rome, Deno and similar.</p><p>When the VC money runs out there will be no one left to maintain them.</p><p>And VC:s sacrifices most companies in the hunt for the truly massive ones, so it’s always more likely that a VC-funded startup will fail than that it will succeed.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
