			"date": "2023-08-29T13:15:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.nintendojo.fr/@meduz\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>meduz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@rich_harris\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>rich_harris</span></a></span> I noted that the structure of Svelte under Vercel is different. As I understand it, Rich is paid full time by Vercel to work on it but it isn't owned by Vercel. And, yes, Vue is afaik funded through sponsorships.</p>",
